  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-5870",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n- a function is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x$ in the domain of $f$\n\n- a function is odd if $f(-x)=-f(x)$ for all $x$ in the domain of $f$\n\nFor our function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-6) & =85=-f(6), \\\\ f(-4) & =75=-f(4), \\\\ f(-2) & =30=-f(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $f(-x)=-f(x)$ for all $x$ in the domain of the function. Therefore, $f(x)$ is an odd function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
